Give Tpetra's Matrix Market I/O header its own include guard.

hypre's _hypre_utilities.h uses the same guard macro, MM_IO_H, but declares its
functions with a hypre_ prefix (hypre_mm_read_banner, hypre_mm_is_valid, ...).
Any translation unit that includes a hypre header before MatrixMarket_Tpetra.hpp
therefore has MM_IO_H already defined, so mmio_Tpetra.h is skipped entirely and
Tpetra's unprefixed mm_* declarations never appear.  MatrixMarket_TpetraNew.hpp
then fails with 'identifier "mm_read_banner" is undefined'.

The two headers define MM_typecode and the MM_MAX_* macros identically, so both
being processed is harmless.

--- a/packages/tpetra/core/inout/mmio_Tpetra.h	2026-09-06 16:06:25.664516148 -0700
+++ b/packages/tpetra/core/inout/mmio_Tpetra.h	2026-09-06 16:06:25.668516105 -0700
@@ -15,8 +15,8 @@
 *
 */
 
-#ifndef MM_IO_H
-#define MM_IO_H
+#ifndef MM_IO_TPETRA_H
+#define MM_IO_TPETRA_H
 
 #define MM_MAX_LINE_LENGTH 1025
 #define MatrixMarketBanner "%%MatrixMarket"
